\section{Introduction} 

The field of computer vision relies heavily on benchmarking neural networks on standard, well-studied datasets, such as ImageNet, CIFAR-10 and CIFAR-100. Our goal was to use basic convolutional nets as baselines on the CIFAR-10 dataset, and then to try to improve on these baselines. Two models were used in this study.

The first model, VGG \cite{vgg}, is a very simple architecture. We have used a VGG-9 architecture, with 6 convectional layers and 3 fully connected layers. Different option were computed. The basic model is the simple VGG-9 with momentum. Then several option where combined between dropout, weight decay, data augmentation and batch normalization. 

Second, the original ResNet \cite{resnet} provides our baseline on CIFAR-10. Our goal was first to match its performance, then add improvements to the network.

\section{Experiments} 

\subsection{VGG}
\paragraph{}
Different models have been trained. We first tried to add dropout layers with prevent from over-fitting. Then we used data augmentation for the model to be more robust, weight decay, and batch normalization. The following table presents the accuracy on the test set. 

